  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 2",
  "description": "Release 2 of the HBN-EEG dataset, the EEG section of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network project, organized in BIDS format. It contains EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 152 participants aged 5-21 years who performed six passive and active tasks: resting state, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning and symbol search. Events carry HED annotations, and the participants file includes quality-control results and psychopathology factors derived from the CBCL.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded while participants performed three passive tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching) and three active tasks (contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files with HED annotations. Minimal quality control checked for file integrity and the presence of required events for each task.",
